/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock
# check.py local scratch: the per-run .out/.time snapshots.
#
# The `.jitstats` baselines beside each benchmark are COMMITTED, synthetic ones
# included. check.py's regression floor reads them on every invocation, so a
# fixture with no committed baseline is not "ungated by default" — it is
# silently ungated, which reads as green. That floor is also the only gate wasm
# has at all: run_synthetic_bench passes vs_pypy=None for wasm, so no perf ratio
# can catch a wasm-only trace-abort storm there.
/check.snap/
